        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nHow do I unlock transmit on more sub-GHz frequencies on Unleashed?",
          "label": "evals/flipper-unleashed/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "ba7aca837b39c96dbb42623036ec7c0d26a6111ac71bddf29d9f3d06699e1932",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "On Unleashed the region locks are already off, so you can select and transmit on frequencies stock firmware blocks. To add frequencies the menu doesn't offer, edit the settings file:\n\n1. On the SD card, find `subghz/assets/setting_user.example` and rename it to `setting_user`.\n2. Add your frequencies, for example `Frequency: 928000000` and `Hopper_frequency: 928000000`.\n3. Reboot the Flipper.\n\nThe CC1101 radio only covers roughly 300–348, 387–464 and 779–928 MHz. Anything outside those bands needs the DangerousSettings switch, which I don't recommend. It's `subghz/assets/dangerous_settings`, changed from false to true. It pushes the radio past its hardware spec and can physically damage it.\n\nWith the locks off, nothing in the firmware stops you from transmitting outside your legal bands or power limits. Only transmit on frequencies you're allowed to use where you are (FCC, ISED, CE or your local equivalent).\n\nI wrote the file names and values from the Unleashed skill notes and didn't check them against the live repo. Compare them with `documentation/SubGHzSettings` in the DarkFlippers/unleashed-firmware repo before relying on them."
        },
        "score": 1,
        "success": true,
