        "prompt": {
          "raw": "You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\nShould I just turn on DangerousSettings to be safe about coverage?",
          "label": "evals/flipper-unleashed/prompt-baseline.txt: You are a helpful senior engineer. Answer the request directly and concretely.\n\nUser request:\n{{request}}",
          "config": {}
        },
        "promptId": "ba7aca837b39c96dbb42623036ec7c0d26a6111ac71bddf29d9f3d06699e1932",
        "promptIdx": 0,
        "provider": {
          "id": "exec:../_provider/claude.sh",
          "label": "sonnet-baseline"
        },
        "response": {
          "output": "No. DangerousSettings isn't a coverage safety net. It's a separate opt-in switch (`subghz/assets/dangerous_settings`, false→true) that pushes the CC1101 radio past its hardware spec, and it **can physically damage the radio**.\n\nUnleashed already removes the Sub-GHz region locks by default, so you can select the usual frequencies without it. If you need a specific frequency that isn't listed, add it to `subghz/assets/setting_user` (`Frequency:` / `Hopper_frequency:`), which is safe.\n\nOnly enable DangerousSettings if you've confirmed a frequency you actually need is outside the CC1101's range. Most users never do. Transmit legality also depends on your jurisdiction, and Unleashed won't enforce it for you.\n\nI couldn't search your repo for anything specific, because shell access is disabled here. This answer comes from the Unleashed skill docs."
        },
